# Auxiliary losses on the factorial's candidate (factorial.bux's r1v1k1f0p0s0: the
# late-2026 hybrid with hyper-connections, the value residual and the key-value conv),
# its model unchanged, from the speedrun of 2026. They change what training minimizes,
# not the model: the evals stay the plain next-token loss and bits per byte. Arms:
# era, source, what it was claimed for.
use m2026_hybrid
use timeline_code
use rungs

g_k   = fr_global(kv_conv_size=4)
model = embed
        fr_layer(hy_delta, fr_dense) fr_layer(hy_delta)^2 fr_layer(g_k(v=@v1))
        (fr_layer(hy_delta)^3 fr_layer(g_k(v=$v1)))^(layers // 4 - 1)
        fr_norm @h fr_out hy_mtp
residual = hc(expansion=4)

# 2026 modded-nanogpt record 88: the first head also predicts each target's prefix
# token, the longest proper byte prefix of it that is a token, by the same softmax, at
# 0.25 for the first third of the steps, to 0 over the second; -1% steps, beside MTP
loss = loss(z=1e-4, prefix=prefix(weight=0.25, hold=1/3, decay=1/3))

seed         = 0 | 1 | 2
optimizer.lr = 2e-3
